"""Collision part 1: loading, rays, volumes, region queries (game/collision.cpp, collision_ray.cpp)

Run: set MUT_HARNESS=collision, MUT_DEFS=-DCOLLISION_QUICK, MUT_EXTRA_SRCS=ls3df/src/math/math.cpp,
MUT_EXTRA_INC=ls3df/src, then python _re/harness/mutrun.py _re/harness/collision/mutations/mutate_collision1.py WORK
[JOBS]. Needs the levels (MISSIONS_DIR). Labels: C collision.cpp, R collision_ray.cpp, + line.
Generated by _re/harness/shots/gen_mutations.py per source (lines unique in their file), merged.

Result (2026-11-11): 869 mutants; 603 killed, 93 not building, 173 survived:
- 102 comparisons at their boundary (< for <=, > for >=, ...): the same unless a value equals the limit exactly,
  which the random rays and the levels' data do not produce (the rays' fractions, the slabs' entries, the cell
  heights, the margins' 1e-8).
- leaks and freeing: C 111, 113, 114, 117, 118 (del, num), 119, 124, 133, 176, 177 (del, num), 178, 187, 199, 201,
  346, 385 (del, num), 473, 474, 483, 488 (state nothing reads, files left open, memory not freed);
- unused: C 58 / 658 / 831 num (array sizes), C 651 (del, num: the volumes-only call's static filter), C 672 (the
  query's unknown4C), R 296 (the ray's end point), R 352 (t, set before use);
- no data: C 237 / 256 (the 0x86 primitive table: no level has entries), C 257 (the capsules' frames: nothing reads
  them);
- the same with any data: C 180 num (the handles start at 1), C 182 num / 197 arith (a mesh block a byte or a file
  longer: the read stops at the end), C 349 / 351 num (one cell either way), C 370 / 372 num (x < 1 sets 0 as x < 0
  does), R 357 num (vertical capsule segments: only one shorter than 1 m going up differs);
- cell ranges one cell wider or narrower within the queries' own margin of a cell: C 533, 534, 685, 687, 689 arith,
  692, 718-721, 764, 765, 767-770 (num, 768 arith), R 210-213, 576, 578, 580;
- early stops (the same hits, more work): R 120 (del, bool), R 624, R 627 bool, R 920 bool.
Runs: the first two (309 and 211 survivors) were void: the test wrote its collision files to fixed names in %TEMP%,
and the runner's six parallel copies overwrote each other's (results flipped both ways). Files are now named after
the process. Added since, from what survived: exact normals and query places of every shape, convex hulls and
capsule primitives, vertical rays at volumes, TestBoxSweep against my own reading of its rules (my levels, BURMA1,
Co_Sicily1, near every kind of primitive), stored kinds that are wrong or missing, the thresholds of the kinds and
of degenerate triangles, levels away from 0 (positive and negative corners), grids that are not square or a single
cell, volumes far outside, the water's range, reused query lists, a segment of length 1, starting inside a sphere or
a hull, the argument checks of dtaOpen / GetLevel / GetVertices.
Checked against the original's asm: RayTestAabb's parallel axes (0x006f46e0), RayTestCapsule's start inside the
infinite cylinder (0x006f4d70), QuerySegment's vertical segments (0x006ff510, jump table 0x00700f60), TestBoxSweep's
squared radius (0x006f0ac0), ClearGrid's emptied cells (0x006eff70); the port matches each.
"""
